# per-case build state, realized by the driver (`mach dep pull` + build)
dep/
out/
# never committed, deliberately: a case's `ref = "branch/main"` tracks mach-std's
# latest release (see doc/cli.md's Lockfile section), so under the default
# `--deps float` this lock's resolved commit is meant to move on every run rather
# than be pinned - committing it would freeze the case to whichever commit last
# happened to be recorded. what a run resolved is recorded instead: in every
# PASS/FAIL/BLESS line (#2387) and in out/deps.txt (#2592). the driver WRITES this
# file in both modes - from the repo's own mach.lock under `--deps pin`, and under
# `--deps float` from whatever the run's first case resolved, so one run is one
# commit (#2619) - which is why it must stay untracked either way.
mach.lock
